$ jailops expose web 80,443 --comment the site
jail/web exposed: 80,443/tcp
  IPv6  2001:db8::10   open: no NAT, the jail's own address answers on 80, 443
  IPv4  10.20.0.10   forwarded: host 80->80, 443->443 (NAT)

$ jailops expose web 80,443 --comment the site
jail/web: the exposure is already what you asked for
  IPv6  2001:db8::10   open: no NAT, the jail's own address answers on 80, 443
  IPv4  10.20.0.10   forwarded: host 80->80, 443->443 (NAT)

$ jailops expose web 8080 --from 192.0.2.0/24 --host-port 9090 --family 4
jail/web exposed: 8080/tcp
  IPv4  10.20.0.10   forwarded: host 9090->8080 (NAT)

$ jailops expose web 53 --proto udp --family 6
jail/web exposed: 53/udp
  IPv6  2001:db8::10   open: no NAT, the jail's own address answers on 53

$ jailops expose --dry-run web 25
jail/web would expose: 25/tcp (dry run, nothing stored)
  IPv6  2001:db8::10   open: no NAT, the jail's own address answers on 25
  IPv4  10.20.0.10   forwarded: host 25->25 (NAT)

$ jailops expose web 22 -o json
{
  "jail": "web",
  "changed": true,
  "entries": [
    {
      "proto": "tcp",
      "ports": [
        "80",
        "443"
      ],
      "comment": "the site"
    },
    {
      "proto": "tcp",
      "ports": [
        "8080"
      ],
      "families": [
        "4"
      ],
